     1	"""P0 nominal native replay REQUEST recorder (isolated and minimal; lineage r24-resume-p0-nominal-v1, UNQUALIFIED).
     2	
     3	Replays one frozen trace_workload schema-1 replay trace against a loopback gateway at ABSOLUTE offered offsets and
     4	records per-request SSE evidence: finish_reason (observed / absent / contradiction), usage, first/last content,
     5	[DONE], HTTP status, fate, request ids and scheduled/sent clocks.  ``normalized_row`` emits the STRICT
     6	``nominal_metrics.ROW_KEYS`` rows with the unchanged r23 natural-SLO fields, so ``build_run`` hands
     7	``nominal_metrics.compute`` a run without another adapter.
     8	
     9	Callers that already own an event loop use ``prepare_capture`` (synchronous local preflight, no HTTP) and then
    10	``await capture_replay`` (the same envelope, replay, rows and summary as the CLI ``replay`` command, without
    11	``asyncio.run`` or signal handlers) and persist with ``write_capture``; the caller's lifecycle owns interrupts.
    12	
    13	Owned by the DRIVER, never by this recorder: model-server / gateway launch, warmup, static budget installation,
    14	final gateway drain, gateway tokenizer and zero-character-fallback checks, full-wall start/end, controller decision
    15	intervals and FIFO/FCFS verification.  No winner, capacity, SLO guarantee or qualification is claimed.
    16	"""
